1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,086
♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor</i> ♪

2
00:00:03,169 --> 00:00:08,425
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

3
00:00:08,508 --> 00:00:10,927
- ♪ <i>Fix this</i> ♪
- ♪ <i>Oh, Mister Tailor</i> ♪

4
00:00:11,010 --> 00:00:14,222
♪ <i>Holding the scissors</i>
<i>Oh, Mister Tailor</i> ♪

5
00:00:14,305 --> 00:00:16,641
♪ <i>One cut, and it's settled</i> ♪

6
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,435
[Samir, in English] <i>Surprised to see me?</i>

7
00:00:18,518 --> 00:00:20,520
Turns out you wronged both me and Samir.

8
00:00:20,603 --> 00:00:21,980
Where are my children?

9
00:00:22,063 --> 00:00:23,189
You won't see them again.

10
00:00:23,273 --> 00:00:24,232
[Atoy] <i>Now I'll finish you.</i>

11
00:00:24,315 --> 00:00:26,651
<i>You're only brave because you</i>
<i>have many people with you.</i>

12
00:00:26,735 --> 00:00:29,696
[grunting, growling, groaning]

13
00:00:29,779 --> 00:00:30,989
‪PREVIOUSLY

14
00:00:31,072 --> 00:00:34,492
[Viktor, in English]
<i>I am looking for Atoy Padua.</i>

15
00:00:34,576 --> 00:00:37,412
[in English] <i>He owes me plenty!</i>

16
00:00:37,495 --> 00:00:38,329
[Martina, in English] This is…

17
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:39,789
Tonet and her brother.

18
00:00:39,873 --> 00:00:41,583
Madame, maybe you're being haunted.

19
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:43,001
That's the one you took out
at the mall, right?

20
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:43,960
[music swells]

21
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:45,128
[Emerson] <i>You animals, all of you.</i>

22
00:00:45,211 --> 00:00:50,425
[grunting and groaning]

23
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:51,926
[Janine] <i>I'm hungry.</i>

24
00:00:52,010 --> 00:00:53,595
That has sleeping pills.

25
00:00:53,678 --> 00:00:56,222
- Huh?
- They want us to fall asleep,

26
00:00:56,306 --> 00:00:58,391
so they can transfer us to the ship.

27
00:00:58,475 --> 00:01:02,228
[grunting and groaning]

28
00:01:02,312 --> 00:01:06,107
[grunts]

29
00:01:06,191 --> 00:01:07,984
- [Gavin] <i>Where's Atoy?</i>
- [Karla] <i>He left. Why?</i>

30
00:01:08,068 --> 00:01:09,277
[Gavin] <i>Someone saw him here.</i>

31
00:01:09,360 --> 00:01:12,280
[in English] She is not Princess.

32
00:01:12,363 --> 00:01:15,158
[man] <i>Who are you?!</i>
<i>What are you doing here?</i>

33
00:01:15,241 --> 00:01:17,535
[grunting and groaning]

34
00:01:17,619 --> 00:01:21,164
[grunting and groaning]

35
00:01:21,247 --> 00:01:22,373
‪[grunts]

36
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:23,666
[Viktor, in English] <i>Who are you?</i>

37
00:01:23,750 --> 00:01:25,919
[in English] <i>You were with Atoy.</i>

38
00:01:26,002 --> 00:01:27,504
[in English] <i>Where is he?</i>

39
00:01:28,671 --> 00:01:30,507
[groaning]

40
00:01:30,590 --> 00:01:32,008
- [gunshots]
- [screaming and panicking]

41
00:01:32,091 --> 00:01:33,510
- [electricity crackling]
- [screaming and panicking]

42
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:36,387
- [gunshots]
- [grunts and groans]

43
00:01:37,263 --> 00:01:38,973
[in English] Yes! Security is breached.

44
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:41,810
- [grunts]
- [gunshots]

45
00:01:41,893 --> 00:01:43,561
[music swells]

46
00:01:43,645 --> 00:01:45,730
- [groans]
- I'm going to kill you!

47
00:01:45,814 --> 00:01:46,689
- [grunts]
- You killed my sister!

48
00:01:46,773 --> 00:01:48,483
- [Karla, in English] No! Let go
- [gunshot]

49
00:01:48,566 --> 00:01:50,610
- [Martina gasps]
- [Red] <i>Atoy is here.</i>

50
00:01:50,693 --> 00:01:52,695
I'm sure he's got company.

51
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:54,239
- Tatoy!
- [Atoy] <i>Child?</i>

52
00:01:54,322 --> 00:01:55,532
Ibyang!

53
00:01:55,615 --> 00:01:56,699
[music fades]

54
00:01:56,783 --> 00:01:58,159
[in English] Stop! Don't move!

55
00:01:58,243 --> 00:01:59,786
[in English] You are all under arrest!

56
00:01:59,869 --> 00:02:01,246
[pensive music playing]

57
00:02:01,329 --> 00:02:04,207
[in English] You cannot arrest me.

58
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:07,752
[in English] I have diplomatic immunity!

59
00:02:08,336 --> 00:02:10,463
[in English] Your president
has waived your immunity.

60
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:11,798
[in English] We can arrest you!

61
00:02:13,842 --> 00:02:15,510
[officer, in English] Men, arrest them!

62
00:02:16,553 --> 00:02:20,056
[grunts, in English] No! No, no, no!

63
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:22,392
- [grunts]
- [tense music playing]

64
00:02:22,475 --> 00:02:24,978
[in English] You can't do this! [grunts]

65
00:02:25,061 --> 00:02:26,688
[in English] Men, move!

66
00:02:37,907 --> 00:02:43,538
[suspenseful music playing]

67
00:02:48,710 --> 00:02:50,003
- Ibyang.
- Tatoy!

68
00:02:50,086 --> 00:02:51,212
Don't move.

69
00:02:51,296 --> 00:02:57,093
[suave theme music playing]

70
00:03:20,617 --> 00:03:22,535
[in English] Ma'am, please stay behind.

71
00:03:23,828 --> 00:03:25,914
Okay. Thank you.

72
00:03:26,956 --> 00:03:29,792
[somber music playing]

73
00:03:30,376 --> 00:03:31,377
[Janine, in English] Mommy!

74
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:33,338
- [heavy music playing]
- Janine?

75
00:03:35,340 --> 00:03:36,841
[gasps] Child!

76
00:03:36,925 --> 00:03:38,134
[in English] Mommy.

77
00:03:39,594 --> 00:03:40,678
[sobs]

78
00:03:41,304 --> 00:03:43,556
[in English] Thank God you're okay, child.

79
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:47,852
[melodramatic music playing]

80
00:03:47,936 --> 00:03:49,187
[Audrey sobs]

81
00:03:51,022 --> 00:03:53,233
Child… [sobs]

82
00:03:53,316 --> 00:03:54,943
Where is Ibyang?

83
00:03:55,610 --> 00:03:59,197
Eh, I don't know where Ibyang is.

84
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:03,034
I even misled the bad guys earlier
so she could escape.

85
00:04:04,285 --> 00:04:06,621
Where is Ibyang, Mommy?

86
00:04:06,704 --> 00:04:09,374
[sharp inhale]

87
00:04:09,457 --> 00:04:13,253
We'll find her, child. Okay?

88
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:24,430
[music fades]

89
00:04:24,514 --> 00:04:26,015
Let my child go.

90
00:04:27,183 --> 00:04:28,685
Face me.

91
00:04:29,560 --> 00:04:31,437
You're something else, Atoy, huh?

92
00:04:32,355 --> 00:04:34,107
You even found us here.

93
00:04:34,732 --> 00:04:36,818
You're a skilled tracker, Master Cutter.

94
00:04:38,778 --> 00:04:40,905
But you've cornered me now.

95
00:04:41,572 --> 00:04:43,116
So, we all go down together.

96
00:04:43,199 --> 00:04:44,117
I'll start with your child.

97
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:45,368
Don't involve my child!

98
00:04:45,451 --> 00:04:46,911
You involved my child!

99
00:04:46,995 --> 00:04:48,538
[dramatic sting]

100
00:04:48,621 --> 00:04:50,039
You brought him here, didn't you?!

101
00:04:52,166 --> 00:04:53,751
He came here because of your viciousness.

102
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:56,254
[Atoy] He wants to stop you!

103
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:59,424
So don't project your immorality
and your sins on me.

104
00:05:00,091 --> 00:05:01,509
Fine, fine.

105
00:05:01,592 --> 00:05:03,052
I'm the worst!

106
00:05:03,136 --> 00:05:04,095
It's all my fault!

107
00:05:04,178 --> 00:05:05,888
[ominous music playing]

108
00:05:05,972 --> 00:05:08,099
So, just accept
that we all go down together.

109
00:05:08,182 --> 00:05:09,350
She goes first.

110
00:05:10,476 --> 00:05:11,936
No, Ibyang.

111
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,438
Don't move, Ibyang.

112
00:05:13,521 --> 00:05:14,897
[Atoy sighs]

113
00:05:14,981 --> 00:05:17,984
Red, don't involve my child.

114
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:21,529
Fine, fine.

115
00:05:21,612 --> 00:05:23,573
I'm the one you want, right?

116
00:05:23,656 --> 00:05:25,283
I'm the one you hate, right?

117
00:05:25,366 --> 00:05:26,784
Fine, take me instead.

118
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:27,994
I'll go with you.

119
00:05:28,911 --> 00:05:30,288
I'll do everything you want.

120
00:05:30,371 --> 00:05:31,831
I won't resist.

121
00:05:31,914 --> 00:05:33,875
Fine. Take me.

122
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:35,960
[heavy breath]

123
00:05:36,544 --> 00:05:38,629
- [Atoy] Huh?
- You're brave, fine.

124
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:40,465
You jump first.

125
00:05:40,548 --> 00:05:42,091
- Fine, fine.
- [Red] Hurry!

126
00:05:42,175 --> 00:05:43,468
Tatoy, don't!

127
00:05:44,635 --> 00:05:46,179
Don't stop him!

128
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:48,431
He's sacrificing his life for you, right?

129
00:05:48,514 --> 00:05:49,807
Don't you want that? You'll live?

130
00:05:50,475 --> 00:05:52,018
Although your Tatoy dies!

131
00:05:52,101 --> 00:05:54,479
[sobs] No!

132
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:57,774
It should be you,
because you're the bad one!

133
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:01,778
You know, my daughter is right.

134
00:06:02,528 --> 00:06:05,198
You're the one who should be eradicated,

135
00:06:05,281 --> 00:06:06,908
because of your savagery!

136
00:06:06,991 --> 00:06:09,077
Then I'll go all out with my savagery.

137
00:06:09,619 --> 00:06:10,828
Tatoy!

138
00:06:10,912 --> 00:06:12,830
[foreboding music playing]

139
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:13,998
[dagger swishes]

140
00:06:14,082 --> 00:06:18,711
[music swells]

141
00:06:19,337 --> 00:06:20,296
[Ibyang] Tatoy!

142
00:06:20,379 --> 00:06:26,636
[tense music playing]

143
00:06:30,181 --> 00:06:32,225
[squeals]

144
00:06:32,308 --> 00:06:33,976
[music continues]

145
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,436
[gasps]

146
00:06:40,191 --> 00:06:41,692
Karla, Karla, wait.

147
00:06:41,776 --> 00:06:43,611
Stay here first. Okay? I'll help.

148
00:06:43,694 --> 00:06:44,654
No.

149
00:06:45,238 --> 00:06:46,823
They told you to stay here, right?

150
00:06:46,906 --> 00:06:48,366
You've already been shot.

151
00:06:48,449 --> 00:06:49,826
No, I'll help.

152
00:06:49,909 --> 00:06:51,035
It's just a graze.

153
00:06:51,119 --> 00:06:52,745
You're really stubborn, huh?

154
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:57,750
Gavin, you don't know anything
about gunfights.

155
00:06:58,668 --> 00:07:00,253
Do you really want to die?

156
00:07:00,878 --> 00:07:01,879
Karla…

157
00:07:03,131 --> 00:07:04,173
I'm alive.

158
00:07:06,342 --> 00:07:09,554
Yes, but you almost died.

159
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:13,224
I don't want anything bad
to happen to you because

160
00:07:13,307 --> 00:07:15,059
you're important to me, Gavin.

161
00:07:17,270 --> 00:07:19,021
Why are you telling me that?

162
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:20,398
You already have a boyfriend.

163
00:07:20,481 --> 00:07:21,774
He's not my boyfriend.

164
00:07:22,650 --> 00:07:24,235
Uno is not my boyfriend.

165
00:07:25,153 --> 00:07:27,280
I only said that to make you jealous.

166
00:07:28,948 --> 00:07:31,576
Because the truth is,
you're the one I really like.

167
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:33,703
I like you, Gavin.

168
00:07:34,996 --> 00:07:38,708
["Sa Wala" instrumental music playing]

169
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:39,709
Really?

170
00:07:42,003 --> 00:07:43,629
Say it again.

171
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:45,298
I just want to be sure.

172
00:07:48,593 --> 00:07:50,970
Yes. I like you.

173
00:07:52,930 --> 00:07:55,391
You're the only one who doesn't like me.

174
00:07:58,352 --> 00:07:59,645
No.

175
00:08:00,521 --> 00:08:02,857
I've liked you for a long time, Karla.

176
00:08:04,275 --> 00:08:06,068
Sorry if…

177
00:08:06,611 --> 00:08:08,988
I realized too late
that you're the one I want.

178
00:08:11,073 --> 00:08:12,492
Even when I was with Cathy,

179
00:08:13,910 --> 00:08:15,328
you were the one I was looking for.

180
00:08:18,414 --> 00:08:19,749
No takebacks, okay.

181
00:08:19,832 --> 00:08:21,083
[soft chuckle]

182
00:08:21,167 --> 00:08:22,793
I'll really punch you.

183
00:08:24,545 --> 00:08:25,713
[in English] Final answer.

184
00:08:27,256 --> 00:08:28,382
I'm sure about you.

185
00:08:29,175 --> 00:08:30,384
[chuckles softly]

186
00:08:30,468 --> 00:08:32,220
♪ <i>If this is just for nothing</i> ♪

187
00:08:32,303 --> 00:08:36,933
♪ <i>No more fooling around…</i> ♪

188
00:08:37,016 --> 00:08:38,518
[groans] Ouch, ouch.

189
00:08:38,601 --> 00:08:40,394
[Karla] Oh, are you okay?

190
00:08:40,478 --> 00:08:42,271
♪ <i>The two of us…</i> ♪

191
00:08:42,355 --> 00:08:43,606
It's just a graze.

192
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:48,236
♪ <i>If this is just for nothing…</i> ♪

193
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:50,112
[music fades]

194
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:52,365
[Emerson] It's Audrey! Audrey!

195
00:08:53,241 --> 00:08:54,534
How did you get here?

196
00:08:54,617 --> 00:08:57,245
I've been waiting
at the mainland for a while.

197
00:08:57,328 --> 00:08:59,872
I found out Mercado's men
were going to attack,

198
00:08:59,956 --> 00:09:02,333
so I looked for a way.

199
00:09:02,959 --> 00:09:05,461
Janine, where's Ibyang?

200
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:08,506
Atoy is probably looking for Ibyang.

201
00:09:08,589 --> 00:09:13,386
[tense music playing]

202
00:09:20,142 --> 00:09:21,727
[Ibyang] Tatoy!

203
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,188
Tatoy!

204
00:09:24,272 --> 00:09:26,065
- Ibyang.
- Tatoy…

205
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:28,150
[music fades]

206
00:09:28,234 --> 00:09:32,446
[sobs] Tatoy… Don't let go, okay!

207
00:09:33,239 --> 00:09:35,992
[sobs] I'll pinch you!

208
00:09:38,369 --> 00:09:40,371
No!

209
00:09:40,454 --> 00:09:44,083
[sobs] I said don't let go!

210
00:09:44,834 --> 00:09:47,378
Just promise me you'll be good, okay.

211
00:09:48,170 --> 00:09:49,297
[grunts]

212
00:09:49,380 --> 00:09:51,007
Wait a minute.

213
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:54,176
[sobs] I'll find a way!

214
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,928
Don't let go, okay!

215
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:59,390
[epic music playing]

216
00:09:59,473 --> 00:10:00,433
Atoy!

217
00:10:00,516 --> 00:10:02,602
- [Uno] Sir Atoy!
- [Kurt] Atoy!

218
00:10:02,685 --> 00:10:03,603
[Uno] Don't let go, okay.

219
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:05,771
- [Paldo] Sir Atoy!
- Here, here!

220
00:10:05,855 --> 00:10:07,898
- [grunts]
- [epic music playing]

221
00:10:08,774 --> 00:10:09,734
[Kurt] Here!

222
00:10:11,402 --> 00:10:12,486
[Kurt grunts]

223
00:10:12,570 --> 00:10:15,740
[Atoy grunts]

224
00:10:16,949 --> 00:10:19,952
[grunts, then groans]

225
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:21,120
[pants]

226
00:10:22,288 --> 00:10:25,374
[Atoy groans]

227
00:10:25,458 --> 00:10:28,794
- [soft drama music playing]
- [Ibyang sobs]

228
00:10:31,756 --> 00:10:34,508
[accessories jingling]

229
00:10:36,385 --> 00:10:37,470
[softly] Thank you.

230
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:40,014
[Atoy, softly] Thank you.

231
00:10:49,607 --> 00:10:55,029
[accessories jingling]

232
00:11:04,121 --> 00:11:05,331
[Ibyang sobs]

233
00:11:06,666 --> 00:11:08,209
My child.

234
00:11:09,960 --> 00:11:11,671
[sobbing]

235
00:11:12,380 --> 00:11:15,716
Good thing you didn't fall.

236
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:18,803
[sobs] If you did,

237
00:11:18,886 --> 00:11:21,222
I'd really pinch you!

238
00:11:22,014 --> 00:11:23,265
[melodramatic music playing]

239
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:27,436
Even at your funeral, I'd still scold you!

240
00:11:28,229 --> 00:11:29,897
- [soft chuckle]
- [sobbing]

241
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,316
Good thing. [soft chuckle]

242
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:39,031
[sobbing]

243
00:11:44,120 --> 00:11:48,791
[Audrey gasps]

244
00:11:49,625 --> 00:11:51,669
Ibyang, child.

245
00:11:51,752 --> 00:11:54,380
[dramatic music playing]

246
00:11:54,463 --> 00:11:58,467
[sobbing]

247
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:21,615
[music fades]

248
00:12:22,741 --> 00:12:24,660
We're incomplete.

249
00:12:24,743 --> 00:12:29,665
[somber music playing]

250
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:49,602
[sobbing]

251
00:12:49,685 --> 00:12:54,315
- [sentimental music playing]
- [sobbing]

252
00:12:57,985 --> 00:12:59,445
Thank you, Saint Anthony.

253
00:12:59,528 --> 00:13:01,822
[sobbing]

254
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:03,949
My family is whole again.

255
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:07,453
[sobbing]

256
00:13:07,536 --> 00:13:11,665
[accessories jingling]

257
00:13:25,846 --> 00:13:28,641
[music fades]

258
00:13:28,724 --> 00:13:33,604
[gentle music playing]

259
00:13:36,315 --> 00:13:40,194
We thank everyone for the support

260
00:13:40,277 --> 00:13:42,655
and the cooperation

261
00:13:42,738 --> 00:13:46,158
of all the agencies
involved in this operation.

262
00:13:47,326 --> 00:13:51,330
How did you find out
that the human traffickers could be found

263
00:13:51,413 --> 00:13:52,414
in Velora Bay,

264
00:13:52,498 --> 00:13:54,833
as well as the number one

265
00:13:54,917 --> 00:13:57,586
wanted bagman in the Philippines?

266
00:13:57,670 --> 00:13:59,713
That also includes locating

267
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,799
the concentration camps

268
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:04,718
of the known terrorist group Obsidian

269
00:14:04,802 --> 00:14:06,095
here in our country.

270
00:14:07,513 --> 00:14:10,182
They say it takes a village

271
00:14:10,266 --> 00:14:11,725
to execute an operation.

272
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:16,730
But the truth is,
it is all because of one man.

273
00:14:16,814 --> 00:14:18,107
[camera shutter snapping]

274
00:14:18,190 --> 00:14:20,609
[in English] A man
who wanted his family back.

275
00:14:22,152 --> 00:14:25,239
[in English] You can have
all the right reasons to do good,

276
00:14:26,323 --> 00:14:30,035
but family is the strongest force

277
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:31,495
to do your best.

278
00:14:31,579 --> 00:14:32,496
[female reporter] Who is he?

279
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:34,164
[in English] May we know his name, sir?

280
00:14:34,248 --> 00:14:35,916
[in English] Is he part of the military?

281
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,543
Where is he now?

282
00:14:37,626 --> 00:14:38,961
[suspicious music playing]

283
00:14:39,044 --> 00:14:40,963
[in English] <i>It's classified information,</i>

284
00:14:42,548 --> 00:14:43,883
<i>but I call him…</i>

285
00:14:46,093 --> 00:14:47,720
<i>The Master Cutter.</i>

286
00:14:47,803 --> 00:14:48,888
[music fades]

287
00:14:48,971 --> 00:14:51,765
[action music playing]

288
00:14:51,849 --> 00:14:54,351
[phone ringing]

289
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:57,771
[Atoy, in English] Are you in position?

290
00:14:58,731 --> 00:15:00,441
- [music fades]
- Copy.

291
00:15:00,524 --> 00:15:02,276
- I'm on my way.
- [phone blips]

292
00:15:02,359 --> 00:15:09,283
[mid-tempo rock music playing]

293
00:15:14,788 --> 00:15:15,789
[Audrey] Where are we going?

294
00:15:15,873 --> 00:15:17,458
[in English] Why did you
make me wear this?

295
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:19,543
[Janine] Because you look beautiful in it.

296
00:15:19,627 --> 00:15:21,837
[Audrey] Where's your daddy anyway?

297
00:15:21,921 --> 00:15:25,799
Hmm, Tatoy left. He has a mission.

298
00:15:26,508 --> 00:15:30,721
So, what we'll do is just pray

299
00:15:30,804 --> 00:15:32,473
that his mission will be successful.

300
00:15:32,556 --> 00:15:33,641
Yes.

301
00:15:33,724 --> 00:15:35,017
[light music playing]

302
00:15:35,100 --> 00:15:37,102
Daddy is really amazing.

303
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:38,354
[in English] Wait.

304
00:15:39,521 --> 00:15:40,606
[in English] What's going on?

305
00:15:41,398 --> 00:15:44,109
[Janine] Hmm, just wait.

306
00:15:44,193 --> 00:15:48,656
[pensive music playing]

307
00:15:48,739 --> 00:15:54,870
[sentimental music playing]

308
00:15:59,625 --> 00:16:01,001
- Um…
- [clears throat]

309
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:02,878
[in English] Wow.

310
00:16:03,545 --> 00:16:04,838
Audrey…

311
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:07,591
Sorry if

312
00:16:07,675 --> 00:16:11,220
I didn't admit to you at first who I was,

313
00:16:12,137 --> 00:16:12,972
and sorry because when…

314
00:16:13,055 --> 00:16:15,766
when we met again,

315
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:18,352
I didn't admit to you my true feelings.

316
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:24,525
But I don't want to be sorry
for not doing this.

317
00:16:31,240 --> 00:16:32,616
Audrey Regalia.

318
00:16:34,159 --> 00:16:35,077
[in English] Will you marry me?

319
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:40,833
[giggles]

320
00:16:40,916 --> 00:16:42,501
[in English] Yes!

321
00:16:42,584 --> 00:16:45,546
- [exclaiming and cheering]
- [sentimental music playing]

322
00:16:45,629 --> 00:16:47,506
- [in English] Yes.
- [in English] Will you

323
00:16:47,589 --> 00:16:49,174
marry me right now?

324
00:16:50,634 --> 00:16:51,885
- Now?
- [Atoy] Now!

325
00:16:51,969 --> 00:16:53,512
[stutters]

326
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:58,225
Yes! Now!

327
00:16:58,308 --> 00:17:03,772
[exclaiming and cheering]

328
00:17:08,318 --> 00:17:10,696
[Father Peping]
We are all gathered here today

329
00:17:10,779 --> 00:17:17,077
to witness the union
of our brother Atoy and Audrey

330
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:21,749
before our Lord
and our patron Saint Anthony of Padua.

331
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:25,461
[music fades]

332
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:30,966
[sentimental music playing]

333
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:33,844
[inaudible]

334
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:41,810
[Ibyang] <i>The Lord is truly amazing,</i>

335
00:17:41,894 --> 00:17:45,606
<i>because He listened to my prayer.</i>

336
00:17:45,689 --> 00:17:51,070
<i>I thought I would grow up without parents.</i>

337
00:17:51,153 --> 00:17:53,989
<i>I thought I would be alone.</i>

338
00:17:54,615 --> 00:17:59,828
<i>But look, I have Tatoy and Mommy now.</i>

339
00:18:00,621 --> 00:18:02,456
<i>I even have a sister!</i>

340
00:18:05,751 --> 00:18:08,337
<i>I'm so happy with my family.</i>

341
00:18:08,420 --> 00:18:10,297
[in English]
And now, you may kiss the bride.

342
00:18:13,383 --> 00:18:18,764
- [music swells]
- [exclaiming and cheering]

343
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:23,393
[sentimental music playing]

344
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:27,106
[all] One more! One more! One more!

345
00:18:27,189 --> 00:18:32,528
[exclaiming and cheering]

346
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:42,204
[all] One more! One more! One more!

347
00:18:42,287 --> 00:18:44,790
[exclaiming and cheering]

348
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:50,003
[light music playing]

349
00:19:03,475 --> 00:19:05,853
[Ibyang] <i>I'm also happy because</i>

350
00:19:05,936 --> 00:19:09,231
<i>our family got to meet</i>
<i>and be with the people</i>

351
00:19:09,314 --> 00:19:11,608
<i>who helped my Tatoy.</i>

352
00:19:13,569 --> 00:19:17,030
<i>They are the ones who are always there</i>

353
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:19,575
<i>and care about him.</i>

354
00:19:20,242 --> 00:19:23,537
<i>Even though Tatoy was grumpy back then,</i>

355
00:19:24,288 --> 00:19:27,291
<i>he already considered everyone</i>

356
00:19:27,374 --> 00:19:29,585
<i>from Tabang Lupa as family now.</i>

357
00:19:29,668 --> 00:19:31,670
[inaudible] What?

358
00:19:31,753 --> 00:19:33,422
[Ibyang] <i>Who would have thought that</i>

359
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:36,133
<i>in the middle of our community</i>

360
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:39,595
<i>there's a tough tracker,</i>
<i>who's also handsome,</i>

361
00:19:39,678 --> 00:19:41,972
<i>like my Tatoy!</i>

362
00:19:42,055 --> 00:19:42,890
[exclaiming and cheering]

363
00:19:42,973 --> 00:19:45,267
- [sentimental music playing]
- [Ibyang] <i>What could his next mission be?</i>

364
00:19:45,350 --> 00:19:48,145
<i>Who will he look for next?</i>

365
00:19:48,228 --> 00:19:49,188
<i>Whatever it is,</i>

366
00:19:50,063 --> 00:19:54,902
<i>the most important thing</i>
<i>we found was each other.</i>

367
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:59,239
